@startuml donor-variants
' Revision 2026-10-13: wave-5 zero-egress admission, R-TRANSFER and controlled verification; formats/qualification unpublished.
' Revision 2026-10-12: R-WORKPLACE service controls, helper-v1 activation and execution-level stops; Draft, no renderer/qualification evidence.
title Donor deployment variants - Draft target: slice 0 + project helper v1/workplace qualification precede donor; A first, B disabled, C sandbox fallback
left to right direction
actor "Human donor\nonly init authority; TTY/typed consent\nis a policy heuristic" as O
node "A - first milestone\nno administrator rights; donor UID" as A {
  component "Curator init / bridge service\nsupervisor, SSH client, signer, admission\nuser service while logged in" as AB
  component "Qualified harness + stdio relay\ndonor UID; no local tool offered\nrelay has no keys/network" as AH
  artifact "Donor-owned state\nkeys, locked config, audit, cursors, budgets\nmanaged home/scratch; release binaries" as AS
}
node "B - future, disabled until separate provisioner spec/qualification\none administrator request" as B {
  component "Separate donor provisioner\nprivileged binary/name/schema pending\nnot swarma-user-manager" as BP
  component "Bridge service\nbridge UID; system daemon survives logout\nsupervisor, SSH client, signer, admission" as BB
  component "Harness + stdio relay\nworker UID; mandatory kernel read sandbox\nper-UID egress; peer-checked relay socket" as BH
  component "Provider proxy\nbridge UID or system service\nqualified provider host allowlist" as BX
  artifact "Bridge-owned 0600 keys/state\nlocked config, audit, cursors, budgets\nworker-owned home/scratch; root-owned releases" as BS
}
node "C - no administrator rights\ndonor UID; sandbox fallback" as C {
  component "Curator init / bridge user service\nsupervisor, SSH client, signer, admission" as CB
  component "Qualified harness + relay\ndonor UID inside sandbox\nhome/scratch writable; runtime read/execute" as CH
  component "Provider proxy\nqualified local proxy; identity role as D1\nno UID split" as CX
  artifact "Donor-owned state/releases\nbridge state outside harness sandbox\nlocked config outside writable set" as CS
}
node "Project host target\nworkplace jobs UID; service controls UID; root-controlled sshd policy" as P {
  component "sshd + relay-only fixed shell\nservice-principal swarma-rb-exec; workplace class\nhelper v1 enforced/applied networking required" as PB
  artifact "Project-owned state\nmailbox; durable effect claims + admission floors\nseparate ten-minute output cache; grants, user KRL\ncarrier credential stays here" as PS
}
cloud "Qualified model provider" as API
O --> AB : choose A; consent / stop / leave / purge
O --> BP : B requires specified and qualified boundary
O --> CB : choose C when rights declined/unavailable
AB --> AH : consumes caller-composed lockdown + remote-auto plan
BB --> BH : consumes plan; launch as worker UID
CB --> CH : consumes plan; apply qualified sandbox
AB --> AS : owns/persists; verifies executable digests
BB --> BS : bridge keys/state; journaled B provisioning/removal
CB --> CS : owns/persists; verifies executable digests
AH --> AB : stdio relay -> local bridge socket
BH --> BB : relay socket; authenticated peer UID
CH --> CB : relay socket; sandbox-only local access
AH --> API : direct provider path; no OS egress guarantee
BH --> BX : only provider proxy; all other egress denied
CH --> CX : proxy + relay only; other IPC/Keychain denied
BX --> API
CX --> API
AB --> PB : donor-originated SSH only
BB --> PB : donor-originated SSH; bridge egress SSH/join only
CB --> PB : donor-originated SSH only
PB --> PS : service-owned controls/claims/audit; keeper holds user CA
note bottom of P
  Every donor variant needs project helper v1 including loopback and backend qualification.
  Jobs: dispatcher/root launcher/start receipt/exec.stop; no same-UID controls.
  Task write scope plan/import bound; OS write boundary = UID writable set.
  Zero egress, denied loopback/no proxy; per-job/runner shape/blast radius unpublished.
end note
note bottom of A
  A has no UID split, sandbox, proxy or OS integrity/confidentiality/egress guarantee.
  A/C: qualified Secure Enclave Macs use non-exportable P-256 signing/SSH;
  0600 files elsewhere. K_enc is separate X25519. B: Ed25519 signing/SSH
  in bridge-owned 0600 files, no Keychain. Algorithms/storage bound to tuple.
end note
note bottom of B
  B absent spec/rules/removal/qualification -> refuse; no substitute helper operation.
  Provisioning failure -> journal undo in reverse order; never retain relaxed rules.
  Every variant: unsupported tuple, changed/unreadable executable, wrong posture
  or policy generation -> refuse; human fixes/requalifies before run.
end note
note bottom of C
  Platform-specific sandbox must be qualified; unknown coverage refuses.
  A availability after B/C qualification unspecified in spec CIP-0009 question 7.
  [[../CIP-0009-donor-side-deployment-and-bridge.md#recommendation CIP-0009 D0-D3]]
  [[../CIP-0008-remote-worker-launch-mode.md#recommendation CIP-0008 R9]]
  [[../../protocol/remote-worker.md#deployment-and-launch-boundary Donor boundary/publication limits]]
end note
note right of P
  R-UNTRUSTED recorded at admission, no subscription lease/binding; slice 0/v0 refuse.
  Host capability matrix + exec profile + zero egress gate every variant; no OS-name ban.
  No shared services beside untrusted placements; join ingress on separate entry host.
  Standing workplace allowed, loop at donor only; R-TRANSFER exact candidate review.
  R-VERIFY heavy work on secret-free ephemeral runners on another machine.
end note
note top of B
  Default no web: donor provider endpoints + our host; lockdown plan disables provider search.
  Trusted-circle opt-in only: qualified provider-search tuple or donor swarma-web.
  swarma-web: own B identity / C sandbox, never harness/bridge; search API only;
  donor search key never crosses channel/package; init consent; results to donor model.
  Both options pending qualification; task resources are read-only with plan digests.
end note
@enduml
